{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide","id":1020857,"title":"Critique on a Red Talon guide","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-22T06:54:43-08:00","id":1020857,"title":"Critique on a Red Talon guide","content":"Basically, my analysis on common Red Talon player issues and how actual wolves act;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/154805735409/critique-on-a-red-talon-playguide\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/154805735409/critique-on-a-red-talon-playguide\" target=\"_blank\"> Not found. </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/154805735409/critique-on-a-red-talon-playguide\" target=\"_blank\"> http://demonsanddogweeds.tumblr.com/post/154805735409/critique-on-a-red-talon-playguide </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T07:16:50-08:00","id":1020867,"title":"","content":"Awesome article.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the whole Alpha/Omega hierarchy isn't true wolf behavior. When I came back to W:tA, I did some research on wolf behavior. What I found was different than what I read when I first started playing Werewolf decade ago. The Wolf Family is very beautiful. Two wolf parents with older siblings looking after younger ones. It must be as difficult for a lupus to have a wolf family as a homid to have a human family. To fight the Wyrm, the Lupus Garou must leave their kin mate to raise their pups alone. <br /> <br /> <br /> I head canon that the Garou rank of &quot;Alpha&quot; is a homid construct. Having a leader that everyone looks up to and a fool that everyone takes their stress out on is something I see in many human social groups. I kind of like the pack structure as it shows Garou are both human and wolf. Actually, we could chalk up a lot of the Red Talon's &quot;flaws&quot; to the tribe denying the influence their homid side has on their actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T09:36:55-08:00","id":1020924,"title":"","content":"My critique on the article, and the whole issue, is actually complex, but let me try it.<br /> <br /> You are completely, undeniably right on the matter of wolf behavior, and how that should affect a Lupus Garou. At most, I would add that the very Litany would be a fairly alien concept to them, and certainly as far from natural and inborn as it is for Homid Garou. The only Garou that should have contact with the Litany from early development in a regular basis are Metis. I agree with everything else, and do thing that wolf-born werewolves should start from this mindset, maybe developing later in a personal manner due to personal experiences, as any sapient being.<br /> <br /> That said, the problem is setting. First, the problem isn't with the players, but with the authors. Players don't see Talons that way because they are ignorant on actual wolves, but because the setting uses Talons, and to a far lesser degree every Lupus, that way precisely. Both the general Talon behavior and the tribe's outlook compound to that, are informed that way in the books, and had implications in setting because of that. Everything of the Talons in the setting derives from such. Second, because of such, to change the tribe to better mirror actual wolves, though theoretically in the spirit of the setting, would be very awkward without some heavy retcons.<br /> <br /> And finally, and you see that I present this as the factor that can explain the actual Talon portrait, make it a logical possibility, not as justifying said portrait as somehow better. But we should always remember that Talons aren't actual wolves. As werewolves, they're fairly intelligent beings from early on, and more susceptible to culture and to more complex cultural constructs. That means that the Talons, as a Tribe, aren't the way they are because they are wolves, but because they are, in a sense, humans. As sentient &quot;human&quot; beings, they can form any cultural concept or bias, including things like heavy prejudice, murderous hate, zealous religious beliefs, byzantine social structures and counterproductive whining behaviors.<br /> <br /> So, its a shame, but the fact remains that the Talons are what the Talons are, and the players think they disruptive for a good reason, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> Personally, though, I disagree with the Talons being a needed counterpoint to the Glass Walkers, though it is a compelling point. They are just &quot;the Lupus tribe&quot; to me, and could be fairly easily replaced by a better and more thorough use of the Lupus breed in other tribes. The GW get very close to this, also, but their approach on the Weaver still remains as a little more deserving as a thing in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T10:16:54-08:00","id":1020939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020924#post1020924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the problem is setting. First, the problem isn't with the players, but with the authors. Players don't see Talons that way because they are ignorant on actual wolves, but because the setting uses Talons, and to a far lesser degree every Lupus, that way precisely. Both the general Talon behavior and the tribe's outlook compound to that, are informed that way in the books, and had implications in setting because of that. Everything of the Talons in the setting derives from such. Second, because of such, to change the tribe to better mirror actual wolves, though theoretically in the spirit of the setting, would be very awkward without some heavy retcons.</div> </div> </div> </div> Please note that the text I critiqued did not come from any books, it was something a fan wrote about how to play a Talon.<br /> The kind of behaviour I reference does not exist in the books, because it would make any scene including it comedic. There have been many MANY cases where a Red Talon player literally started arguing with a higher ranked NPC over something, alone. And it naturally stalled the scene down. The fact that the guide encouraged this behaviour was the main reason I actually wrote this thing. Because whether or not it fits the view of the tribe, it also makes having a Talon in the game a bother and a drag. And as such I tried to explain the reasons why to avoid this kind of behaviour for the sake of any STs' sanity. That is where the wolf perspective came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020924#post1020924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And finally, and you see that I present this as the factor that can explain the actual Talon portrait, make it a logical possibility, not as justifying said portrait as somehow better. But we should always remember that Talons aren't actual wolves. As werewolves, they're fairly intelligent beings from early on, and more susceptible to culture and to more complex cultural constructs. That means that the Talons, as a Tribe, aren't the way they are because they are wolves, but because they are, in a sense, humans. As sentient &quot;human&quot; beings, they can form any cultural concept or bias, including things like heavy prejudice, murderous hate, zealous religious beliefs, byzantine social structures and counterproductive whining behaviors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, Talons are not just wolves. But they have in a very real way stunted any chance they could to comprehend the more complex brains they have. Hence the xenophobia, rage and culture they enforce.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020924#post1020924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, its a shame, but the fact remains that the Talons are what the Talons are, and the players think they disruptive for a good reason, unfortunately.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, major issue didn't come from the books per se. Just players being stupid with their Talons and thinking arguing about everything with everyone is how to play one. Best Talons I've seen have followed orders and focused on the pack rather than spend hours of RP arguing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020924#post1020924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, though, I disagree with the Talons being a needed counterpoint to the Glass Walkers, though it is a compelling point. They are just &quot;the Lupus tribe&quot; to me, and could be fairly easily replaced by a better and more thorough use of the Lupus breed in other tribes. The GW get very close to this, also, but their approach on the Weaver still remains as a little more deserving as a thing in the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Granted, Red Talons are not written to capitalize on that. But given how they are placed in the order of tribes hints this. After Glass Walkers come Red Talons in every corebook. Human vs Wolf, in essence. But you are right that they should have been written better to match it.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:17:19-08:00","id":1020986,"title":"","content":"Granted, players are unusually able to take stereotyped visions about things and make everything ever worse. I saw players that do such with every tribe: Skin-head Fenris, Hysterical Furies, Backstabber Lords, Mad-eye Fangs, and so on, and so forth. You name it, someone found a disruptive way to do it.<br /> <br /> But the game isn't innocent on that behavior. It is the game, with description and tone, that lays the ground for this behavior and its likely intensity and frequency. Disruptive Fenris are more common than disruptive Fangs, disruptive Uktena aren't as common as disruptive Wendigo, a seriously stereotyped Glass Walker isn't as disruptive as a seriously stereotyped Shadow Lord. And from all this, the Talons are the worst. They are the most common and most disruptive in a general basis (of course, groups and individuals can experience variations), and yes, the game is to blame, simply because it doesn't help.<br /> <br /> Lets see, surely the game discourages strongly that any Talon goes against its superiors. <i>Directly</i>. But the Talons <u>are</u> frequently depicted as resentful from the pro-human view of most superiors. The tribe lives in the wild as much to stay with the Wyld as it is to avoid the other tribes and sects, so they don't have to deal with superiors they don't agree with and don't want to listen to. It is pretty childish to me. They are eager to blame the Silver Fangs on everything they do because &quot;they were following the Alphas, as good wolves&quot;, but also resent and avoid them. The game puts the structure and religion of the Garou Nation on them, as alien as it is for true wolves, and them makes them among the most zealous about it. Of course, except when they don't want to, since they are as hypocritical as everyone else.<br /> <br /> So, if there is a mistake in this disruptive interpretation of the Talons, it is because almost all Talons are either isolationists or passive-aggressive, or both, and the others are considered weird by their peers. Yes, a Talon can be incredibly distinct from this and be both well integrated into other septs and capable of dealing with humans, it isn't any overt crime for them. But it is considered weird and frowned upon. Again, passive-aggressive to the core. Packs are family. A passive-aggressive a***ole, or a depressive member who's being bullied by its own tribe, aren't that better to make things work (but a little, indeed).<br /> <br /> And to make things better, there's Griffin. If this totem was truly about the wild, and living as an animal, I would say nothing. It goes, however, further in xenophobia and hate.<br /> <br /> Yes, Talons could be better defined to be the counterpoint of GW. They wouldn't, though. Even the GW could have a better work, though they are in a far better shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T13:36:57-08:00","id":1020992,"title":"","content":"Not terribly helpful to the discussion at hand, but...<br /> I find it interesting how many problems people on here have had with the Talons. I've never been in a group where these issues have come up. Until the few threads on here that I've read outlining a number of problems with the Tribe/Talon players, I would never have thought of some of these.<br /> <br /> For example:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020986#post1020986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> it is because almost all Talons are either isolationists or passive-aggressive, or both, and the others are considered weird by their peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience, most Garou are pretty isolationist. I've not really encountered passive-aggressive behavior from players (or seen it in the fiction from Garou), outside of one RL couple in my first gaming group that was having relationship problems and taking it out on each other in game. But that certainly has nothing to do with the game as written. And I think a great deal of PCs might be &quot;considered weird by their peers&quot;. Not all, but in general that sort of thing comes with being a PC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1020986#post1020986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And to make things better, there's Griffin. If this totem was truly about the wild, and living as an animal, I would say nothing. It goes, however, further in xenophobia and hate.</div> </div> </div> </div> Griffin is problematic at times, but there are one or 2 other Totems that suffer similarly. With Griffin though, it's not like he/it is going to punish a Talon for being in a pack with Homids. So the Totem's personal outlook doesn't play as heavily into a Talon PC's outlook necessarily.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T14:10:43-08:00","id":1021000,"title":"","content":"As I said, there are bound to be personal experiences that are exceptions. I personally never had a player even interested in the Talons.<br /> <br /> I see the passive-aggressive stance most on the tribe as a whole. In the fiction their aggressiveness is either overt or they're not there. Or the one Talon being shown isn't shown dealing with the tribe. But there are fiction I didn't saw, so, who knows.<br /> <br /> Yes, PCs can be considered weird more often than not. But the game doesn't usually requires it, and there are level for it. Most PCs are weird, but mostly able to participate in social dynamics of their tribe. Those Talons are weird in a tribe that take it even less lightly, and their less aggressive response seems to be.<br /> <br /> The problem with isolationism is that most tribes keep a reasonable level of contact with other tribes. They get in touch with the Garou Nation to a reasonable degree. The next more isolated are the Wendigo, and not even them are as isolationists as the Talons. Given how they recognize other tribes' roles and the Silver Fangs as Alphas, something isn't adding up.<br /> <br /> Griffin isn't the only problematic totem, not even for a tribal totem. But it is bad, and adds to what is already a bad situation. And the very fact that it isn't the worst only serves to break any justification that it is its influence. Less Furies hate men than Talons hate humans, and Pegasus isn't my favorite, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:20:21-08:00","id":1021034,"title":"","content":"Obviously not arguing, just recounting my own experience with the game (I feel this sort of thing needs saying, since text online is so easy to misinterpret).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1021000#post1021000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In the fiction their aggressiveness is either overt or they're not there.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has generally been my experience with players (and actually, with NPCs I've seen in other's games). But with players, the aggressive disagreements are usually ironed out in the first few sessions as the characters determine where they stand with each other and then the pack works a lot smoother together.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1021000#post1021000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, PCs can be considered weird more often than not. But the game doesn't usually requires it, and there are level for it. Most PCs are weird, but mostly able to participate in social dynamics of their tribe. Those Talons are weird in a tribe that take it even less lightly, and their less aggressive response seems to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, not my experience. But I guess I can see that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1021000#post1021000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The problem with isolationism is that most tribes keep a reasonable level of contact with other tribes. They get in touch with the Garou Nation to a reasonable degree. The next more isolated are the Wendigo, and not even them are as isolationists as the Talons. Given how they recognize other tribes' roles and the Silver Fangs as Alphas, something isn't adding up.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Talons do keep a reasonable level of contact with the Nation (when I agreed to them being isolationist, I thought you meant towards the outside world, not towards other Garou). They're a small Tribe, so obviously you are going to run into them less often. But that being said, they are usually accounted for in supporting Garou leadership and said leaders count on them in the various fictions to show up when called. I think Nation-Talon relationship has weakened a lot in the modern days due to the Garou being overwhelmingly Homid now, but in times passed I don't think there was any divide at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1020857-critique-on-a-red-talon-guide?p=1021000#post1021000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Griffin isn't the only problematic totem, not even for a tribal totem. But it is bad, and adds to what is already a bad situation. And the very fact that it isn't the worst only serves to break any justification that it is its influence. Less Furies hate men than Talons hate humans, and Pegasus isn't my favorite, either.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree completely. My only point was in setting, a Tribal totem not liking something doesn't make or break relationships the Garou of that tribe can have.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:59:34-08:00","id":1021058,"title":"","content":"Talons aren't <u>completely</u> isolationist. But you see, they're around usually only when called for. Most cosmopolitan septs don't count so much with Talon presence, nor their caerns are very open for Homid. And you see, every other tribe have at least some caerns that are open to visiting members of other tribes. Sure, there are secret caerns, but there's also open ones. Except for the Talons. Not even the Furies have only caerns closed to men (and, in fact, male Metis are a thing among the Furies). Wendigo are the next, as I said, and they have contact with the Nation and the Old Brother in far more ways. Even them have caerns where they accept to meet foreigners. Sometimes. And even let them live on 1 out of 3 occasions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T16:59:21-08:00","id":1021071,"title":"","content":"Why do you think there aren't open Talon Caerns? I'm not sure if this is a thing stated somewhere, unless their Tribebook says this specifically (it may, it's been years since I've read through it). I certainly wouldn't assume it. I can see the Talon enforcing a Lupus form only restriction (combat excluded) to visitors, but I don't see them outright banning all foreigners. Form restrictions aren't unprecedented. The Strider Caern Wheel of Ptah&quot; strictly enforces a homid form restriction, even on Talons.<br /> <br /> And most cosmopolitan Septs don't have Stargazers either. It's not because they aren't welcome or don't want to be there. I think it's just a numbers thing. One of the signature caerns, Sept on the Green, was a cosmopolitan Sept with a Talon in residence. I know one example doesn't mean so much, but it's one of the few multi-tribal Caerns we have as a canon example.<br /> <br /> In any case, I doubt the Talons have more than a handful of Caerns (there should only be a few hundred Talons worldwide). Of those, I would guess only 1 or 2 are closed, which is about normal for most Tribes. My impression of them, is that there are certainly Caerns where humans are killed on sight. I just don't see Talon Caerns killing outsiders (Garou) on sight.<br /> <br /> And I'm obviously open to being corrected via citation from the books. These are just my impressions/understanding on the Red Talons in general.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T17:54:48-08:00","id":1021090,"title":"","content":"I don't like the MET wiki thing, but I think some of the critiques are lacking as well.<br /> <br /> One thing is that the &quot;wolf behavior thing,&quot; is an issue, but at the same time Garou operate more like wolves in zoos than they do like wild wolves. A Garou pack isn't a wild wolf back. It isn't parents and a few generations of sibilings with maybe some aunts and uncles. A Garou pack is a bunch of individuals that are brought together without the continuity of family that makes wild wolf packs so different from what people used to think about wolf behavior. Lupus in general have to deal with a major disconnect between the idea of a pack that they grew up in, and the idea of a pack that the Garou live in. The structure of Garou hierarchy at all levels operates differently from normal wolves, and there's going to be a struggle dealing with it (and trouble for homids too).<br /> <br /> I also think there's a bit of uncharitable reading in insisting that the MET wiki article is trying to say that Talons are constantly physically fighting for dominance. The article in question mentions staredowns as well (keeping in mind that there are only three standard challenge types in the game: combat, staredown, and gamecraft). Staredowns should be very common for younger lupus still trying to figure out their place in the strange and unique thing that is Garou society; even if they're expecting to lose most of them. As well, wolves do use physical punishments frequently to correct behavior. Lupus are going to be very used to short bursts of violence as higher &quot;ranking&quot; individuals putting others back in line. As Garou they're a lot tougher than a normal wolf, so the idea that they'd be a bit more ready to be rough and tumble than homids makes perfect sense (and they'd likely be very confused by homids that insist on a more human/thoughtful approach to corrective measures).<br /> <br /> Of course, I think we all know that I'm not a fan of the Talons in general. My experiences with them being banned/restricted in online games or LARPs is a bit more expansive than either article really addresses. Part of it is the books themselves, but a lot of it is just that Red Talons that work well in a large Sept with most Tribes represented end up eating most/all of the lupus population and deny it to other players, while frequently either being too important or too inconsequential to what's going on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T19:30:26-08:00","id":1021112,"title":"","content":"You see, we have only one true opinion here: Talons could and should be better portrayed, be it by players/STs or by the books themselves.<br /> <br /> I'm game to work on a better description, though, and I do agree with Ana Mizuki's article as a start, anyway. My problem resides on seeing the same problems in the books, not in disagreeing that they are a problem, or that things have unavoidably to be that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T23:06:05-08:00","id":1021169,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, a player is still responsible for making sure everyone has fun and that they don't derail the game. Even if the books say it should go that way, a player should take responsibility to make sure what they do fits the game at hand.<br /> <br /> Hence the rather heavy handed points about dominance and such XD<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T05:15:01-08:00","id":1021231,"title":"","content":"In my perspective, Red Talons are constantly fighting a battle of Weaver (human) versus Wyld (wolf) within themselves, and it colors their perspective. Neither human nor wolf have the same battle and, in the case of wolves, survival matters more than existential crises. A wolf can except a human as equal and, from time to time, will adopt humans into the pack (early researchers into wolf behavior were often surprised with how accepting wolves could be of humans when the wolves determined they were no threat to the cubs). Red Talons lack the pragmatic flexibility of wolves because they reject anything that they associate with humans, but humans and wolves share many features, so they inevitably reject some of the Wolf as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T06:02:36-08:00","id":1021244,"title":"","content":"They &quot;reject&quot; everything of a true wolf in the moment they decide to take up the fight for Gaia, to reject humanity on the basis of tradition, to care for things in the big picture. They go all right away of how true wolves think. The Talons make the weird and extremely complex mental exercise of going away from how wolves <i>actually are</i>, because they clearly can't be the same, and embrace the wolves as an idea, pretty much as the GW do with humans.<br /> <br /> Well, what the Wyld represents for such a tribe? Why they choose to culturally remain wolf-like and reject humanity while embracing their transformation in a sapient thing?<br /> <br /> A Garou that truly wants to keep as a wolf isn't in it for a better time than the madmen that reject it to remain human. They wold go pretty crazy just for their cognitive ability, and definitely reject any aspect of the werewolf mindset and the Umbra. So the Talons have to be something more than simply &quot;we like wolf, don't like non-wolf&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}